{#-
  BLOCK: masthead — §06's `masthead`, as Design's 5th package draws it: a
  solid 60px band in the brand colour with the brand name (or the email logo)
  left and the date right, then the kind · area · period line on white.

  SOLID, AND THE ACCENT IS GONE. The band used to be a primary-to-accent
  gradient with text on it, chosen against both stops (`_on_band`). Design
  removed the gradient and with it the only use of the accent in the email,
  which also removes text-on-gradient from the product's rules. `bgcolor` and
  `background` both carry the fill: `bgcolor` is what Outlook paints.

  `on_primary` is the text colour ON the brand fill (themes.derive_theme). The
  fill itself is the agent's colour and never moves.
-#}
          <tr><td bgcolor="{{ primary }}" style="background:{{ primary }};font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;"><tr>
            <td class="tr-pad" style="padding:18px 28px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">{% if logo_url %}<img src="{{ logo_url }}" alt="{{ brand_name }}" style="display:block;max-width:160px;max-height:32px;width:auto;height:auto;border:0;">{% else %}<span style="font-size:16px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:{{ on_primary }};">{{ brand_name }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td align="right" class="tr-pad tr-hide" style="padding:18px 28px;text-align:right;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:12.5px;color:{{ on_primary }};">{{ date_label }}</span></td>
          </tr></table></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="tr-pad" style="padding:26px 28px 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><span class="tr-muted" style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#64748B;">{{ kicker }}</span></td></tr>
